      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_determineinterventions",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Determine appropriate digital health interventions"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 4. Select interventions for the prioritized challenges, assess whether the enabling environment can support them, identify functional requirements and user stories, map the future-state workflow, and check whether existing applications already meet the requirements. The interventions CONSIDERED AND NOT CHOSEN are part of the output, with why — `methodology-adoption`'s fourth refusal. A deleted alternative leaves the next reader unable to tell a decision from an oversight. Selection is from the Classification, and the `who-digital-health` voice governs the naming: an intervention is a capability, not the software that delivers it."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_DetermineInterventions",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_DetermineInterventions",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_developbudget",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Develop a budget"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 7. Phases of implementation, cost drivers, and the budget matrix. This is the chapter that turns the preceding six into a COSTED implementation plan, which is the artefact the whole Guide exists to produce and the one a funder reads."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_DevelopBudget",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_DevelopBudget",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_formteam",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Form the team and establish goals"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 2. Determine roles and responsibilities; develop a common understanding of the health programme's needs and goals; understand programme operations across levels of the health system."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_FormTeam",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_FormTeam",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_linkenterprisearchitecture",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Link to the enterprise architecture"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 6. Assess the digital health enterprise architecture, identify the common and enabling components and shared services that make up the digital health platform, and link the investment to both."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_LinkEnterpriseArchitecture",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_LinkEnterpriseArchitecture",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_mapcurrentstate",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Map the current state and confirm bottlenecks"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 3.1. Determine the health programme processes to target, map their workflows, identify and confirm bottlenecks. Then 3.2, a root cause analysis. This is where DIIG builds on CRDM, and it says so: \"This process builds on the Public Health Informatics Institute's Collaborative Requirements Development Methodology (CRDM)\". Its three areas of concentration are business process analysis, business process redesign and requirements definition — two of which name diagrams this platform already executes. They are parallel tracks, not a composite: pick one per decision and name it."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_MapCurrentState",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_MapCurrentState",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_monitorandusedata",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Monitor, and use data effectively"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 8. Establish a logic model, plan the monitoring and evaluation, establish a culture of data use, and manage adaptively — using the data to optimize the interventions rather than only to report on them. The full treatment of this chapter is a separate publication in this library, `9789241511766-eng`, Monitoring and Evaluating Digital Health Interventions. It is a parallel track, not a sub-step: do not blend the two."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_MonitorAndUseData",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_MonitorAndUseData",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_planimplementation",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Plan the implementation"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 5. Infrastructure; legislation, policy and compliance, including data management, privacy and security, and the regulation of new technologies; leadership and governance, including external partnerships; workforce and training; services and applications."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_PlanImplementation",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_PlanImplementation",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_prioritizebottlenecks",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Prioritize, and map to health system challenges"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapters 3.3 and 3.4. Prioritize the bottlenecks, then map the programme-specific ones onto the generic health system challenges. THE ARITHMETIC IS REFUSED HERE. DIIG Table 3.3.1 asks three questions, each scored 1-3 — how much impact does this bottleneck have on the process, what is the likelihood of overcoming it, is it important to a wide range of stakeholders — and sums them into a Score and a Prioritized Ranking. The three criteria are adopted whole; the total is not. Record each criterion's answer AND its reason, and order by argument. A ranked list reads as evidence in a way three stated judgements do not, and the weights were invented."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_PrioritizeBottlenecks",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_PrioritizeBottlenecks",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_valueproposition",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/smart-base/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Make the value proposition and set next steps"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 9. The case made to whoever pays, and what follows. Scaling up is a different method and a different publication — `9789241509510-eng`, The MAPS Toolkit — which begins where this implementation ends."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_ValueProposition",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_ValueProposition",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
